Not res:// content. This directory is the addon's PACKAGE project: its sources compile into
Paradise.Godot.Editor.dll and reach Godot as an assembly reference, never as script resources.

Without this file Godot imports all ~20 .cs here as scripts and mints a .cs.uid beside each one -
noise at best, and actively confusing for the two types whose design depends on NOT being res://
scripts: AuthoredEntityNodeBase (the shim under addons/paradise/ is the registered global class)
and ParadiseExportPluginBase (plugin.cfg points at the shim, not at this).
